{"name":"Pink Blessing","hex":"#f2a9ba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"blessing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Some kind of divine or supernatural aid, or reward.","A pronouncement invoking divine aid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of bless"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blessing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blessing","blocks":[{"text":"In religion, a blessing is the impartation grace, holiness, spiritual redemption, or divine will upon a person, object, or endeavor. It can be nonverbal or verbal, and entails various components: the act, its content, the means, the bestower, and the receiver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%9F%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%BE%D0%B1%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%A1%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B3%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BB%D1%8F%D0%B5%D1%82_%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE_%D0%BA%D0%BD%D1%8F%D0%B7%D1%8F_%D0%94%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%8F_%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B2%D1%8B%D1%81%D1%82%D1%83%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B5_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%B2_%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B8_%D0%9C%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%8F_01.jpg/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blessing","wikidata":"Q626510"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white i